Time Complexity:
O(m × n)

Space Complexity:
O(m + n)

Approach:
1. Create two HashSets to store row indices and column indices containing zeroes
2. Traverse the entire matrix
3. If a cell contains 0, store its row and column index in the respective HashSets
4. Traverse the matrix again
5. If the current row or column exists in the HashSets, set that cell to 0
6. Continue until all cells are processed



class Solution {
    public void setZeroes(int[][] matrix) {
        HashSet<Integer> rowZero = new HashSet<>();
        HashSet<Integer> colZero = new HashSet<>();
        int m = matrix.length;
        int n = matrix[0].length;
        for(int i=0; i<m; i++){
            for(int j=0; j<n; j++){
                if(matrix[i][j] == 0){
                    rowZero.add(i);
                    colZero.add(j);
                }
            }
        }
        
        for(int i=0; i<m; i++){
            for(int j=0; j<n; j++){
                if(rowZero.contains(i) || colZero.contains(j)){
                    matrix[i][j] = 0;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
